  "Question": "A random sample of 5 parts has lengths (mm) of 10, 10, 11, 10, 9 (with a mean of 10). Calculating the sample variance as “the mean of the squared differences between each data value and the mean,” what is the sample variance? (Write as a decimal.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "0.4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The sample variance is $[0+0+1+0+1]\\div5=0.4$.",
